{
  "id": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
  "featureId": "ebb9ceb0-ea12-4374-af6e-12aa4256bcc3",
  "number": 78,
  "shortId": "37HYB",
  "priority": 17,
  "slug": "plugin-ui-gaps-close-the-declarative-model-s-capability-gaps-make-the-translator-self-maintaining",
  "title": "plugin-ui-gaps: Close the declarative model's capability gaps + make the translator self-maintaining",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "All nine tasks done (2026-07-27). The declarative model's capability gaps are closed and the translator maintains itself: layout and visual settings are separate and self-describing, widget-specific settings are generated with a drift test, Input placeholder + ScrollRegion axes are reachable, Separator and the interactive Row joined the vocabulary, appearance is an ordinary property with the theme as default, and the published docs match the code. T009 finished it by moving the model into `heca-view` (serde only) and `realize` into `heca-view-realize`, both below the app — which is what finally lets the showcase render a described tree, closing the verification gap that had made every earlier task in this phase unviewable. Looking at it immediately found a real widget defect (an inset state highlight could be shorter than its content), fixed in the library with a guard test.",
  "description": "═══ WHY THIS PHASE EXISTS ═══\n\nSplit out of F003/P011/T006 (typed builder SDK) on 2026-07-25, after research the user asked for.\nT006 was going to build a typed builder on top of the CURRENT prop vocabulary. That would have\nfrozen a set of holes into a compile-checked API — the builder would make it *impossible* to write\na padding, which is worse than today's silent ignore. This phase corrects the model first; T006\nthen builds the typed builders on top of a corrected model.\n\n═══ THE CORE DEFECT ═══\n\n`heca/src/chrome/realize.rs` hand-writes a reader for every property, per widget. When someone adds\na builder to a widget in `heca-grid-ui`, nothing forces the matching reader to be added. It has\nbeen forgotten repeatedly. The capability exists in the widget and is unreachable from a\n`ViewNode` — silently, with no warning, no log, no test failure.\n\nVerified by listing every property-name string literal `realize.rs` actually reads and diffing it\nagainst the widgets' real builder APIs (2026-07-25, on main @ d698916).\n\n═══ THE FULL GAP LIST (each verified in code) ═══\n\nREAL GAPS — the widget can do it, a ViewNode cannot say it:\n\n1. `padding` (and `justify`, `width`, `height`, `direction`, margins, spacing tokens).\n   `realize_flex` (realize.rs:440-459) reads ONLY `gap` and `align`. Everything else on `Style`\n   is unreachable. NOTE: the original design doc writes `Column::new().gap(8).padding(12)` at\n   docs/chrome-and-ui.md:340 — the very line introducing the builder SDK. Padding was\n   intended from day one and simply never got a property. This is an oversight, not illustration.\n\n2. `Input` placeholder. `Input::placeholder()` exists (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/input.rs:122) and\n   the showcase uses it twice, including the command palette (showcase.rs:264, 698). The realize\n   arm (realize.rs:163-176) reads only value + `name` + change intent.\n\n3. `Scroll` axes. `ScrollRegion` supports both axes: `new()` (vertical), `horizontal()`, `both()`,\n   `axes(ScrollAxes)` (scroll_region.rs:186-247). The showcase depends on it — its entire root is\n   `ScrollRegion::new().both()` (showcase.rs:1897) plus a `.both()` grid demo (showcase.rs:1401).\n   realize maps `WidgetKind::Scroll` to a bare `ScrollRegion::new()` (realize.rs:133), so anything\n   declarative is vertical forever.\n\n4. The clickable `Row` widget is unreachable, AND ITS NAME COLLIDES.\n   `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/row.rs` is a focusable, clickable container — hover tint, active\n   marker with `ActiveMarker`, press flash, focus ring, `on_activate` (mouse + Enter/Space),\n   described as `Item`'s open cousin for rich clickable dock rows.\n   `WidgetKind::Row` does NOT map to it. It maps to `Flex::row()` — a plain horizontal box with no\n   interactivity (realize.rs:124). Two different things share one name, and the interactive one has\n   no declarative spelling at all. docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 2 writes exactly this\n   (`Row::new().gap(12)...on_press(intent(...))`) against a kind that cannot do it.\n\n5. `Separator` has no `WidgetKind`. The widget exists (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/separator.rs —\n   `horizontal()`, `vertical()`, `length()`); the vocabulary has no entry. docs/chrome-and-ui.md\n   example 2 uses `Separator::new()`.\n\n6. `PropValue::Color` is DEAD. Declared in the model (view.rs:201-202, documented as \"#rrggbb /\n   #rrggbbaa, or a theme color token name\") and read by NOTHING — grep of realize.rs finds only\n   `glyph_prop`, never a colour reader. Either wire it to theme token names or remove it.\n\nDOC ERRORS — the docs promise things that have no native equivalent either:\n\n7. `Panel::new().title(\"Hello\")` (docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 1, README). There is no Panel widget:\n   `WidgetKind::Panel` realizes to a plain `Surface` (realize.rs:129-131, comment says so), and\n   `Surface` has no title (surface.rs — only `new`/`row`/`column`). `Card` is the titled one.\n\n8. `Label::new(..).variant(Variant::Muted)` (docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 2). `Label` has no variant\n   natively (label.rs — align/color/bold/italic/underline/strikethrough/font_size/font_scale), and\n   `ViewVariant` is button-shaped: Primary, Secondary, Destructive, Outline, Ghost, Link — no\n   Muted (view.rs:169-176). Muted text is a COLOUR, which ties this to gap 6.\n\n═══ THE PLUMBING DECISION (user-driven, 2026-07-25) ═══\n\nThe user rejected \"just add the missing readers\": adding a reader per property means the next\nproperty is forgotten too. They also rejected a single `apply_style_props()` function, correctly\nnoting it STILL needs a line per new field — it moves the drift, it does not remove it.\n\nAgreed direction: the property list must BE A TYPE that a generator reads, never a function body\nsomeone remembers to update. That splits by layer:\n\nLAYER A — layout settings. They do not live on the widgets. They all live on one `Style` struct\n(heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs:211) hanging off `Base`, which every widget embeds. Make `Style`\n(the layout part) able to read and write itself, then merge a node's properties into it. Add a\nfield later and it works with zero code anywhere.\n  PRECEDENT ALREADY IN THE CODE: `realize` (realize.rs:100-112) already applies `align_self` and\n  `justify_self` generically for every kind, with the comment \"read it once here rather than in\n  each arm\". The right pattern was started and not finished — that is exactly why `gap` works only\n  inside `realize_flex` while `align_self` works everywhere.\n\nLAYER B — settings that belong to one widget (placeholder, axes, checked, severity, value). These\nare fields on individual widget structs; nothing generic reaches them. A small code generator over\nthe widgets' own builder methods writes the translation.\n\nAfter both, realize.rs contains NO property-name list at all and cannot fall behind.\n\n═══ BLOCKER ON LAYER A: `Style` MIXES LAYOUT WITH VISUALS ═══\n\nA whole-struct merge would hand plugins raw colours. `Style` holds `fill`, `border`, `glow`,\n`accent`, `fg`, `radius` (style.rs:289-295) in the same struct as `padding` and `width`.\n\"Styling is not a property — the plugin picks intent (danger/accent/size), the host resolves the\nactual pixels from the Theme\" is rule C of docs/chrome-and-ui.md §2.6.1 and is repeated\nin AGENTS.md's SETTLED table (\"Is styling a prop? NO\").\n⇒ The layout/visual boundary must become a TYPE, not a reviewer's memory. See T1.\n\nAlso note: `heca-grid-ui` currently has NO serialization dependency at all — its dependencies are\nheca-core, heca-theme, floem_reactive, taffy (heca-grid-ui/Cargo.toml:8-12), and `Style` derives\nonly `Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq` (style.rs:210). Layer A adds that, plus derives down through\n`Length`, `Align`, `Justify`, `Direction`, `Spacing`, `WidgetSize`, `GridCell`.\n\n═══ SETTLED CONSTRAINTS — DO NOT RE-OPEN (AGENTS.md:730-796) ═══\n\n- `heca (app) ──depends on──▶ heca-grid-ui (library)`. NEVER the reverse.\n- `heca-grid-ui` must NOT own `ViewNode`, and `Button::new(ViewNode)` is impossible.\n- `realize` is the ONE ViewNode→widget bridge, app-side.\n- Behaviour crosses as an `Intent` (action id + args), never a callback.\n- Styling is not a property; semantic variant/size/align + colour/glyph NAMES only.\n- A widget whose state is a live host signal is HOST-ONLY (`ScrollBar`; also individual builders\n  like `DockFrame::rail(..)`).\n- Any code generator added for Layer B must keep `heca-grid-ui` free of `ViewNode`: the library\n  may only gain a NEUTRAL scalar type, never the app's model.\n\n═══ WHAT HAPPENS AFTER THIS PHASE — F003/P011/T006 RESUMES ═══\n\n⇒ **The typed builder SDK is F003/P011/T006. It STAYS in F003/P011 — it was NOT moved here.**\nOnly the model corrections live in this phase. T006 is the consumer that motivated them.\n\nT006 status: `planned` (set back from `in-progress` on 2026-07-25 — it was started, then this phase\nwas split out of it; nobody is working on it).\n\nSTART T006 WHEN: T1-T8 of this phase are done. T9 is DEFERRED and is NOT a prerequisite — it is a\nrecorded question for the WASM phase, not work.\nThe three decisions T006 needs, all settled here rather than there:\n  - T6 — how the interactive row is named (it determines the builder type name).\n  - T7 — whether a description may name a theme colour (it determines whether a colour builder exists).\n  - T2/T3 — the final property names, since each typed builder method maps to one.\nT006's own shape was already researched on 2026-07-25 and needs no re-deriving: per-kind types with\nshared traits, plain names behind a module (they collide with the native widget names that\nrealize.rs imports), all 30 kinds, guarded by a coverage test modelled on `WidgetKind::ALL`. The\nspelling is fixed by three documents that already agree — docs/chrome-and-ui.md §2.6.1\n(line ~252) and §2.6.2 (line ~340), docs/chrome-and-ui.md examples 1-3, and README.md's Plugins\nsection.\nNOTE on T006's description: its line \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\" cannot be literally true while the\nmodel lives in the app crate. See T9.\n\n═══ OPEN QUESTION, DELIBERATELY NOT DECIDED HERE ═══\n\nFor a Rust plugin to get editor suggestions, the builder types must live somewhere a plugin can\ndepend on. Today the model is inside the app (`heca/src/chrome/view.rs`) and a plugin cannot depend\non the app. The workspace has six members and none is a plugin kit\n(Cargo.toml:2 — heca-core, heca-renderer, heca-config, heca-grid-ui, heca, heca-theme); the plan\nnever names one either. This is NOT the thing AGENTS.md forbids (that rule is about pushing the\nmodel down into heca-grid-ui) — a separate small crate alongside is a different question. But it is\nthe only way F003/P011/T006's sentence \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\" can ever be true. Recorded as\nT9 (deferred), and CROSS-REFERENCED into the phase that must answer it: F003/P001 (plugin-08: WASM\nplugin runtime) and its T1 (Design WASM host API facade).\n\n═══ WHY IT MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS ═══\n\nNothing in an editor ever showed an author what was available — a property is a piece of text, and\nno editor can suggest text. That is HOW the holes stayed hidden. `.prop(\"padding\", PropValue::Int(12))`\nlooks completely correct, is the obvious thing to write, has no effect, and nothing reports it.\n\n═══ RELATIONSHIP TO OTHER WORK ═══\n\n- F003/P011/T006 (typed builder SDK) — the follow-on. See the dedicated section above.\n- F003/P011/T007 (Table widget) — deferred 2026-07-25, unrelated. No consumer; the task is\n  explicitly \"on demand\".\n- F003/P011/T008 (author docs) — the docs are already written and complete; T8 here corrects the two\n  errors in them plus the stale BACKLOG.md pointer.\n- F003/P001 (plugin-08: WASM plugin runtime) — carries T9's question; cross-referenced both ways.\n\n═══ MANDATORY ON EVERY TASK (AGENTS.md:811-819) ═══\n\nWhenever a widget OR the declarative model (ViewNode, props, Intents) is touched, BOTH must be\nupdated in the same change: (1) full rustdoc on the type/fields/methods — never reduce to a bare\npointer; (2) `docs/widgets.md`. The props-by-kind table in view.rs's rustdoc (view.rs:311-337) and\nthe matching section in docs/widgets.md are the two places that must stay in sync.",
