    },
    {
      "id": "1ea732ca-3582-44f4-be02-245375910948",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 309,
      "shortId": "RL7LK",
      "priority": 3,
      "shortName": "generated-translation-for-widg",
      "title": "Generated translation for widget-specific settings + a drift test that fails on a missing one",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Layer B of the plumbing decision. Independent of T1/T2 (which handle layout) but shares their goal:\nrealize.rs must stop containing a hand-written list of property names.\n\nCURRENT STATE\nSettings that belong to ONE widget — placeholder, scroll axes, checked, on, severity, value,\nselected, expanded, active, frameless, nav_selected, dismissible, action_text, body — are fields on\nindividual widget structs. Nothing generic reaches them, so `realize_kind`\n(heca/src/chrome/realize.rs:114+) hand-writes an arm per kind, each naming its properties as string\nliterals. When a builder is added to a widget, nothing forces the arm to be updated. That is how\ngaps 2 and 3 (placeholder, scroll axes) happened.\n\nWORK\n- Add a uniform setter to `heca-grid-ui`: a trait along the lines of\n  `fn set_prop(&mut self, key: &str, value: PropInput) -> bool`, plus a small code generator that\n  writes the implementation from the widget's own annotated builder methods.\n- `realize_kind` then shrinks to: construct the widget for the kind, then feed it the node's\n  properties. No property names in the app.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINT (AGENTS.md:739-746, SETTLED)\n`heca-grid-ui` must NEVER see `ViewNode`, `PropValue`, or anything else from the app — the app\ndepends on the library, never the reverse. The library may only gain a NEUTRAL scalar type\n(bool / int / float / text / enum-name). The app converts `PropValue` into it at the boundary. If a\nproposed design needs the library to know an app type, the design is wrong — stop and re-plan.\n\nOPT-OUT IS REQUIRED, NOT OPTIONAL\nSome builders bind closures or live signals and CANNOT come from static data. These are host-only\nby design and must be excluded from the generator, not merely undocumented:\n- `on_click` / `on_activate` / `on_change` — behaviour crosses as an `Intent`, never a callback.\n- Signal-bound builders, e.g. `DockFrame::rail(..)` (documented as host-only in docs/widgets.md:1704).\n- The whole `ScrollBar` widget (view.rs coverage note: host-only, plugins use `Scroll`).\nGetting this wrong would let a description claim a capability that silently does nothing — the exact\ndefect this phase exists to remove.\n\nTYPE MAPPING\nBuilders take varied argument types: `impl Into<String>`, `f32`, `bool`, `Glyph`, `ButtonVariant`,\n`ScrollAxes`, `ToastSeverity`, `LabelSide`. Scalars are direct. Enums arrive as NAMES (consistent\nwith how glyphs and colours already work in the model) and need a name→value conversion per enum —\ngenerate that too, or the enum list becomes the new drift.\n\nTHE DRIFT TEST (the real deliverable)\nA test that walks each widget's generated property table and fails when a native builder has no\ndeclarative counterpart and no explicit opt-out marker. Model it on the existing coverage guard\n`every_widget_kind_realizes_to_a_live_widget_except_the_host_only_ones`, which already stops a new\n`WidgetKind` from silently rendering an empty container (AGENTS.md:775-778).\nThis test is what would have caught `Input::placeholder` and the scroll axes years ago. It is worth\nmore than the generator itself — if the generator proves too costly, KEEP THIS and report back\nrather than shipping neither.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- realize.rs holds no property-name string literals for widget-specific settings.\n- Adding a builder to a widget without exposing it or marking it host-only FAILS the build.\n- Host-only builders are excluded by an explicit marker, and the markers are documented.\n- Full workspace green, clippy clean.\n- Update view.rs's props-by-kind table + docs/widgets.md.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-26 — commits 94b1a2e, fc653b4, 58cef57, 7ff13d3, c74f3d3, de5656c.\nUser verified in the showcase after the realize rewiring: no visual change.\n\nWHAT LANDED\n1. New crate `heca-grid-ui-macros` (syn/quote): `#[props]`, `#[prop]`, `#[host_only(\"reason\")]`,\n   and a `PropName` derive. `#[props]` on an impl block generates `SetProp` from the builders\n   inside it, so a widget's own builders ARE its declarative surface.\n2. `heca-grid-ui/src/prop.rs`: neutral `PropInput` (Bool/Number/Text) + `SetProp` + `PropName`.\n   The library still never sees ViewNode/PropValue — the crate graph is untouched.\n   `extern crate self as heca_grid_ui` in lib.rs so generated paths resolve inside the library.\n3. `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs`: `with_props` + `prop_to_input` — the ONE conversion at the\n   boundary. realize.rs now contains ZERO widget property names. `bool_prop`, `f32_prop` and\n   `align_prop` deleted (no callers left).\n4. Drift guard `heca-grid-ui/tests/prop_drift.rs` — reads the widget sources, fails when an impl\n   block full of builders has no surface. Found NINE widgets the annotation pass had missed on its\n   first run, plus a stale entry in its own exceptions list. `NO_SURFACE_REQUIRED` is an\n   EXCEPTIONS list (fails closed) and a second test fails when an entry names a type that no\n   longer exists.\n\nORDER — USER REQUIREMENT, ENFORCED NOT DOCUMENTED\n\"I don't want users / developers / agents to think about order when developing.\"\n`#[prop(late)]` was designed and then REMOVED. Properties are applied AFTER children are attached,\nwhich dissolves the only real dependency (Select/Tabs clamp `selected` against the option count).\n`#[prop]` now REJECTS ANY ARGUMENT at compile time with an explanation, so a sequencing hint\n(`late`, `after = \"..\"`) cannot be reintroduced one widget at a time. Verified the error fires.\n\nCLASSIFICATION IS NEVER IMPLICIT — USER REQUIREMENT\n\"we need to expose all properties the same way a single widget does.\"\nA builder must be `#[prop]` or `#[host_only(\"reason\")]`; neither = build failure. 168 builders\nclassified: 93 props, 75 host-only. The host-only reasons ARE the answer to \"what is unreachable\":\n  22 closures (behaviour crosses as an Intent) · 19 composed content (use `children`)\n  12 no value to carry · 8 COLOUR (dated gap → F003/P017/T7) · 4 live host signals\n  2 multi-argument builders · 1 unsupported arg type (impl Into<Option<f32>>)\nThree categories are principled; colour is a real gap pointing at the task that closes it.\n\nGAPS DELIBERATELY LEFT (not oversights — each is recorded in code):\n- Colour: 8 builders marked host_only with \"reachable once F003/P017/T7 makes appearance\n  overridable\". T7 flips them to `#[prop]`.\n- Multi-argument builders (`Overlay::panel_size(Length, Length)`): the macro maps ONE argument.\n  Either split the builder or extend the macro — not decided.\n- `char` and `impl Into<Option<f32>>` argument types unmapped.\n- The drift guard checks impl-block level; per-builder classification is enforced by the MACRO\n  instead, which is stronger. Both together mean nothing is unclassified.\n\nFLAGSHIP GAPS CLOSED, WITH TESTS: `Input::placeholder` and `ScrollRegion` axes are now settable\nfrom a ViewNode (`a_description_can_now_set_an_inputs_placeholder`,\n`a_description_can_now_ask_for_a_two_axis_scroll_region` in realize.rs). Both existed in the\nwidgets for months and no description could reach them. This also closes most of T4.\n\nBUG WORTH REMEMBERING: the first marker check used `path().is_ident(\"prop\")`, which does not match\n`#[heca_grid_ui_macros::prop]` — every marked builder was silently demoted to host-only and the\ngenerator produced an empty surface that looked like it worked. Now matches the LAST path segment.\n\nDEFAULTS CHECKED BEFORE REWIRING: the old arms used `unwrap_or(true)` for `expanded` and\n`unwrap_or(false)` for `checked`; both match the widgets' constructor defaults, so feeding only the\nproperties a node carries is behaviour-preserving. `DockFrame::frameless()` became `frameless(bool)`\nso it could be a property; one showcase call site that looked affected was a `Pane`, not a\n`DockFrame`.\n\nVERIFICATION: 915 tests green, clippy --all-targets --all-features --locked -D warnings exits 0,\nshowcase builds, user confirmed no visual change.\n\nDOCS (both mandatory places): view.rs rustdoc + docs/widgets.md now state that the builders are the\nauthority and the props-by-kind table is a reader's summary, plus the order-independence guarantee\nand what is deliberately not a property.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
