    {
      "id": "0223c291-8cba-4ca0-8712-6ade0e8d0aed",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 310,
      "shortId": "8RLW9",
      "priority": 4,
      "shortName": "expose-the-two-proven-missing",
      "title": "Expose the two proven-missing widget settings: Input placeholder and Scroll axes",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Closes gaps 2 and 3 of the phase description. These are the two concrete cases that revealed the\nwhole defect, so they double as the proof that T3's generator works.\n\nSEQUENCING\nDo this AFTER T3. Once the generator lands, each of these should reduce to marking the existing\nbuilder plus a test — if either still needs a hand-written arm in realize.rs, T3 is incomplete and\nthat is the finding to report.\nIf T3 is dropped or deferred, this task still stands on its own as two hand-written arms.\n\nGAP 2 — Input placeholder\n- Native: `Input::placeholder(impl Into<String>)` exists at heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/input.rs:122.\n- In use: showcase.rs:264 (the command palette — \"Type a command…   (↑/↓ · Ctrl+J/K · Enter)\") and\n  showcase.rs:698 (\"CALLSIGN\").\n- Declarative: the realize arm (realize.rs:163-176) reads ONLY the value via `text_of(node)`, the\n  `name` binding for form submission, and the change intent. No placeholder. A description cannot\n  produce an empty input that tells the user what to type.\n- Note the naming trap: `Input` uses `text` for the VALUE (view.rs props table: \"`Input` | `text`\n  (value), `name`\"). The placeholder needs its own key; do not overload `text`.\n\nGAP 3 — Scroll axes\n- Native: `ScrollRegion::new()` is vertical; `horizontal()`, `both()` and `axes(ScrollAxes)` exist\n  at scroll_region.rs:231-247. `ScrollAxes` (scroll_region.rs:101) has `is_vertical`/`is_horizontal`.\n- In use and load-bearing: the showcase's ENTIRE root is `ScrollRegion::new().both()`\n  (showcase.rs:1897), plus a `.both()` grid demo (showcase.rs:1400-1401).\n- Declarative: realize.rs:133 builds a bare `ScrollRegion::new()`. Every declarative scroll area is\n  vertical forever. A horizontal or two-axis region cannot be described at all.\n- The property carries an ENUM by name (vertical / horizontal / both), matching how glyph and colour\n  names already travel in the model. Unknown name ⇒ keep the widget's default (vertical), never panic.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Realize stays TOTAL: a missing or mistyped value leaves the widget's own default in place.\n- Do not disturb `ScrollRegion::new()`'s deliberate constructor settings (min sizes Px(0.0),\n  flex_shrink Some(1.0), pad_spacing_y, gap_spacing — scroll_region.rs:188-214). See T2's warning:\n  apply on top of the constructed widget, never rebuild from defaults.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- A ViewNode can set an input's placeholder and a scroll area's axes.\n- Tests for both, including the unknown-enum-name and wrong-type cases.\n- The declarative form is verified to match the native one — same widget, same behaviour.\n- Update view.rs's props-by-kind table + docs/widgets.md (§Input, §ScrollRegion).\n- Scroll axes are visible behaviour: build it and have the USER confirm a two-axis declarative\n  region actually scrolls both ways. Green tests are not verification here.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-26, verified by the user in the app.\n\n## The finding the task asked for: T3's generator made both FREE\n\nNeither gap needed code. `Input::placeholder` (input.rs) and `ScrollRegion::axes` (scroll_region.rs)\nwere already `#[prop]`, and both realize arms already ran `with_props`, so a description could set\nthem the moment T3 landed. T3 is complete, not short.\n\n## What this task actually added\n\n- **Two end-to-end tests through `realize` itself** (heca/src/chrome/realize.rs). The tests T3 left\n  called `with_props` directly, which proves the surface exists but not that the arm wires it:\n  - `a_realized_input_paints_the_placeholder_it_was_given` — reads the result the only way a\n    `Box<dyn Component>` allows, by painting it and looking for the run.\n  - `a_realized_two_axis_region_is_the_native_one` — a described region produces a scene IDENTICAL\n    to `ScrollRegion::new().axes(Both)` with the same content; unset matches the vertical default;\n    an unknown axis name keeps vertical through the whole path.\n  - `a_realized_two_axis_region_consumes_a_horizontal_wheel` — routing, not just geometry: the\n    described two-axis region consumes a horizontal wheel delta, the default one does not.\n- **Docs.** `view.rs`'s props table and docs/widgets.md both gave `Scroll` no props at all and listed\n  `Input` as `text`/`name` only. `Scroll` now documents `axes`; §ScrollRegion's declarative note said\n  axes were host-side, which had become false; §Input documents `placeholder` under its own key with\n  the reason it is not `text`. Folded §Input's duplicated \"From a plugin\" heading into one.\n- **Two doc-comment slips** from T3's accessor insertion: `Input::placeholder`'s and\n  `ScrollRegion::axes`'s doc lines had landed on the new `placeholder_str` / `clone_axes` getters,\n  leaving both builders undocumented.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe user confirmed a described two-axis region scrolls both ways, in a modal body (the only surface\nin the app that realizes a `ViewNode`). The showcase cannot host this: `realize` lives in `heca` and\nheca-renderer must not depend on it. A temporary demo body was used and has been removed.\n\nThat verification also uncovered the two real bugs behind this phase's sibling work: the app was\nnever delivering `Scroll` or `PointerReleased` to a modal layer. Tracked and fixed under F004/P011.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [
        {
          "id": "0223c291-8cba-4ca0-8712-6ade0e8d0aed-check-001-expose-input-placeholder-under-its-own-key-do-not-overload-text-which-is-the-value",
          "title": "Expose Input placeholder under its own key — do NOT overload `text` (which is the value)",
          "checked": false
        },
        {
